  ],
  "text": "There is a tree in California that was already ancient when the pyramids went up. Four thousand eight hundred and fifty years old, and its location is kept secret. You can only date it by drilling out a core the width of a pencil and counting. But in Utah there is something that makes even that tree look young. Forty seven thousand separate trunks. All of them one single organism. One root system under the ground, connecting every stem to every other. So which is the oldest tree? It depends entirely on what you call an individual. By one definition it is five thousand years. By another it is tens of thousands. The hard question was never how old. It is where one tree actually stops. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
